    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` as a **derived field** computed at DTO-mapping time, matching the existing pattern for the other computed read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than storing redundant data. Since the value is fully determined by the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, there's no reason to persist it or touch the service/schema layers.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it in the API response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression and a small single-responsibility helper:\n   ```java\n   default String formatMembershipNumber(Owner owner) {\n       if (owner == null || owner.getCustomerCode() == null || owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {\n           return null;\n       }\n       return String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100);\n   }\n   ```\n   The `%02d` zero-pads the last two year digits, so a 2026 registration with code `SMI-0007` yields `SMI-0007-M26` (and e.g. year 2007 \u2192 `-M07`), exactly per the spec. Null guards mirror the sibling formatters so the mapper is safe before the fields are assigned.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` passing.",
